 rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the description (2026-11-09 15:20 PST): the harness does NOT exit on this error. The 12:21 PST run (pid 27240) printed the 'cannot list .tickets-tracker' line and kept running, making model calls for 3 hours. The error is a non-fatal line on stderr, so the observed defect is a misleading error message emitted before the run proceeds, not an aborted run. Which call emits it is still untraced. The reproduction steps showing a second run proceeding after a CLI call are unaffected; the claim that the first run stopped was wrong.","timestamp":1794266176936456001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Manual check (fresh `make worktree` checkout fix-4e0a-harness-mount, 2026-11-17 10:55 PST): before, `.tickets-tracker` was absent and the model-facing `show_ticket('d45f-229f-effe-4cf8')` returned `Error: ticket system not initialized`. After `provider_parity.main(['--slot','standard','--limit','1','--epochs','1'])` ran with a stubbed `run_slot`, `.tickets-tracker` is a symlink to `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker`, and the same call returns the ticket JSON. The new unit tests fail against origin/main's src (2 failed: mount not called) and pass with the change (65 passed in both modules).","timestamp":1794941801572084828},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3417 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged as e6b9f8f849bc2717ec4d42bb7a4d634d59af4549. `make verify` exited 0 on f1f55fed321: 21348 passed, 30 skipped; integration tier 222 passed, 2 skipped. Still unresolved and not needed for this fix: which call emitted the exact \"cannot list\" line at 872e7f6c3fd. It did not reproduce across 27 real items at 83ca81e709e.","timestamp":1794952768516291628}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794258352458117001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"af3aa9d7-e9c8-4aeb-9681-3c963eef485b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"},{"link_uuid":"8d491105-baee-42db-8502-e30c81489d18","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8a29-a7e8-4a41-4b9f"}],"description":"## Problem\n`python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity` (the operator-run parity harness) printed the following in a fresh worktree created by `make worktree` (2026-11-09, origin/main 872e7f6c3fd):\n\n```\nError: cannot list '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker': [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker'\n```\n\nThe run continued and made model calls (see the 2026-11-09 correction comment). The message went away once any `rebar` CLI command had run in that worktree, because the CLI creates the `.tickets-tracker` symlink.\n\n## What is established (2026-11-17 PST, origin/main 83ca81e709e, worktree with no `.tickets-tracker`)\n- **provider_parity's tracker reads depend on whether an earlier CLI call attached the store.**\n  - Plan-review criterion cases run on the in-place checkout. `_run_criterion_case` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:101-148`) uses no `case_store`, and calls `resolve_gate_config(repo_root)` with `repo_root=None`.\n  - The agentic runner gives every such finder the model-facing `show_ticket` tool on `cfg.tickets_path or cfg.repo_path` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:385-396`, `rebar_tools` at `src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py:263-289`).\n  - Called directly in this worktree with a full id, an 8-digit short id, an alias and a `rebar:` token, that tool returns `Error: ticket system not initialized. Run 'ticket init' first.` every time.\n  - So in an unattached worktree, every criterion finder that retrieves a ticket with `show_ticket` gets an error instead of the ticket, and the measured verdicts depend on worktree state.\n- The exact \"cannot list\" line comes from `rebar._ids._scan_tracker_root` / `_scan_alias` (`src/rebar/_ids.py:268-272`, `:452-456`) when `os.listdir(tracker_dir)` fails. That line did not reproduce at 83ca81e709e. A print hook that dumps a stack on any \"cannot list\" line saw none across 27 real harness items:\n  - 1 full `main --slot standard --limit 1 --epochs 1` run, both arms;\n  - 1 `run_arm` over each of the 16 distinct plan-review criterion solvers;\n  - 1 `run_arm` over each of the 10 distinct code-review solvers.\n\n  So the specific emitter on 872e7f6c3fd's path is not identified. The fix below does not depend on it, because it removes the missing-tracker state that every such read hits.\n- **Why the CLI does not hit it.** The CLI dispatcher calls `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` (`src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:387`, defined at `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py:149-178`) before any command. In a linked worktree it symlinks the main repo's tracker (`init_core` \u2192 `_init_via_symlink`, `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:541-598`), never creates a first store, and never raises. The `python -m` harnesses do not go through the dispatcher.\n- **The sibling harness `python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` has a narrower dependency.**\n  - Its `review_plan` runs against a disposable `case_store` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:288-307`, `repo_root=store`), so it does not read the checkout tracker.\n  - The one checkout-tracker read is `_tracker_title` (`:244-256`), which calls `rebar.show_ticket(ticket_id)` inside `except Exception: return None`.\n  - In an unattached worktree, `row_title` (`:259-269`) therefore silently falls back to the first prose line instead of the real ticket title. That changes the titles recorded in the comparison output.\n\n## Approach\nGive both operator harnesses the same store-mount step the CLI uses, at the point where a real run starts. In each `main()`, after the `--dry-run` (and, in provider_parity, `--probe`) early returns and before any model call, call `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()`. Dry-run and probe stay side-effect-free.\n- This reuses the CLI's own consent-free attach rules unchanged: mount an existing store by symlink or branch attach, never create a first store, never raise.\n- No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py`: in `main` (`:583`), call `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` after the `--probe` and `--dry-run` returns and before `run_slot`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`: in `main` (`:441`), call it after the `--dry-run` return and before `run(...)`, so `_tracker_title` reads the real title.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` and `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py`: tests that monkeypatch `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` with a recorder and stub the run (`run_slot` / `run`) to record call order.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a non-dry-run `main` records the mount call before the first run call, for both harnesses.\n- Edge path: `--dry-run` records no mount call (both harnesses), and `--probe` records none (provider_parity).\n- Existing tests in both test modules still pass.\n- Manual check, recorded on this ticket: in a fresh `make worktree` checkout, the `show_ticket` tool returns \"ticket system not initialized\". After provider_parity's `main` has run with a stubbed `run_slot`, `.tickets-tracker` is a symlink to the main store, and the same tool call returns the ticket's JSON.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Both harnesses mount the existing tracker the way the CLI does before a real run, and not on `--dry-run`/`--probe`. Checked by the new unit tests.\n- [x] In a fresh worktree, the manual check above shows the symlink created and `show_ticket` returning the ticket, recorded on this ticket.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0 on the change.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py","reason":"mount the existing tracker before a real run, as the CLI does"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py","reason":"same mount step for the sibling harness"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py","reason":"mount-before-run and dry-run/probe no-mount tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py","reason":"mount-before-run and dry-run no-mount tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8a29-a7e8-4a41-4b9f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"eab00250-164b-43eb-8af4-2fa235d5c161","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4e0a-0d78-ecac-4656","ticket_type":"bug","title":"provider_parity harness fails in a fresh worktree until a CLI call attaches .tickets-tracker","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d9efbeaf-8ee0-41f4-ae5f-1260bcc03356","9a953617-08c5-443b-9eb1-2c6812b0f0e5","458e201f-1f5f-4018-9af0-a37332930fc5","5bb87250-adb5-4c32-9f1d-a0520dfcb5d8","c03baf4f-e2fc-4744-aeee-a6b32eed32e1","7c258899-f22c-4d57-8cde-564881ef92fd","1a867dc8-73ba-4b06-bda8-e6411c223553","9f389ef4-a61f-43a0-a40b-14e56d185f40","8d491105-baee-42db-8502-e30c81489d18","5001bd40-90ad-4999-9e6d-d5fc317451c0","9ff55ce4-6f57-413c-ae29-cce6b58cc3d6","da6ff27a-e1d1-4fd5-a30e-d7bb35e7d4ad","eab00250-164b-43eb-8af4-2fa235d5c161","38f740cf-7a6e-4b38-9854-583cc0afa719"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794952957132061338,"uuid":"da4b5270-08ec-4c1d-a887-eaffdf622ff1"}
